---
title: Suggest an entry
description: Suggest an event for the timeline. Every submission is reviewed by a person before it appears.
---

<div class="wrap">

  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Contribute</p>
    <h1>Suggest an entry</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Spotted something missing? Send it over. Every submission is read by a
      person before it appears — nothing goes live automatically.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-2" style="align-items:start">

    <section class="card" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
      <h2 id="how-heading" style="font-size:1.075rem;margin-top:0">How to submit</h2>

      <p>
        Suggestions are handled as GitHub issues — a structured form with a box
        for each field on the timeline.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg"
           href="https://github.com/{{ site.repo }}/issues/new?template=timeline-entry.yml"
           rel="noopener">Open the submission form &rarr;</a>
      </p>

      <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:1rem">
        You'll need a GitHub account, which is free to create. It's what lets us
        reply to you about an entry and credit the contribution.
      </p>

      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem">What happens next</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Your suggestion arrives for review. Nothing is published yet.</li>
          <li>A maintainer checks the date and the source.</li>
          <li>If it holds up, it's approved — and appears on the timeline within
            a few minutes, automatically.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="small muted">
          If something needs changing first, we'll comment on your submission
          rather than quietly editing it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card" aria-labelledby="good-heading">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 id="good-heading" style="font-size:1.075rem;margin-top:0">What makes a good entry</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>A source of record.</strong> Link the body that actually
            holds it — the governing federation, the legislation, the archive,
            the agency. That's the single biggest factor in whether an entry is
            accepted. An encyclopedia link is accepted, but it publishes with an
            <em>unverified</em> marker until someone finds a primary source.</li>
          <li><strong>An honest date.</strong> If it's approximate, write
            <code>c. 1600 BC</code> rather than claiming a precision the record
            doesn't have.</li>
          <li><strong>A short detail.</strong> One or two sentences. The tooltip
            is small, and long text gets trimmed.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem">Dates the timeline understands</h3>
        <p class="small">
          <code>1896</code> · <code>1948-07-29</code> · <code>July 1948</code> ·
          <code>776 BC</code> · <code>AD 79</code> · <code>c. 3000 BC</code>
        </p>
        <p class="small muted">
          Add an end date only for things that lasted — that draws the event as
          a bar rather than a point.
        </p>

        <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem">Which track?</h3>
        <p class="small">
          Pick one of the {{ timeline.categories | length }} existing tracks if it fits, or
          describe a new one and we'll place it. Current tracks:
        </p>
        <p class="small muted">
          {% for cat in timeline.categories %}{{ cat.name }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</div>
